    <p class="eyebrow">4TH MAY GAMES</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-date">Last updated: 6 November 2026</p>

    <p>This Privacy Policy explains what information <strong>{{ site.legalName }}</strong> (“we”, “us”, or “our”), a company registered in the Republic of Korea, collects when you play our mobile games and use our website, what we do with it, and who we share it with.</p>
    <p>It applies to every mobile game we publish on the App Store and Google Play, including any game released after the date above, and to this website at <a href="{{ site.url }}">{{ site.url }}</a>. Together these are referred to as the “Games” and the “Site”. Our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a> cover the rules for using the Games.</p>

    <h2>1. What information we collect</h2>
    <p>We aim to collect as little personal information as possible. Most of what we collect does not identify you by name, although some of it may uniquely identify the device you play on. What is collected differs from Game to Game.</p>

    <p><strong>Device and usage information</strong>, collected automatically in most Games:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>(i) information about your mobile device, such as make, model, operating system version, language, time zone, country, and your device’s advertising identifier;</li>
      <li>(ii) information about how you use the Game, such as which features you open, session length, in-game progress events, and whether you interacted with a notification;</li>
      <li>(iii) diagnostic information, including crash reports, error logs, and performance data;</li>
      <li>(iv) your IP address, which is also used to infer your approximate location at country or region level. We do not collect precise GPS location.</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Game progress and account information</strong>, in those Games that offer a cloud save or sign-in feature:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>(i) your in-game progress, settings, and inventory;</li>
      <li>(ii) an account identifier, and where you sign in through a third-party service such as Google Play Games or Sign in with Apple, the identifier that service gives us. We do not receive your password.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Games without such a feature keep your progress only on your own device, and we never receive it.</p>

    <p><strong>Information you give us directly</strong>, such as the content of an email you send to our support address, including your email address and anything you choose to tell us about your device or your problem.</p>

    <p><strong>Purchase information.</strong> When you make an in-app purchase, Apple or Google processes the payment and tells us that a purchase was completed so we can deliver the item. <strong>We never receive or store your payment card details.</strong></p>

    <h2>2. How we use this information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To run the Games, deliver purchases, and save or restore your progress where that feature exists;</li>
      <li>To find and fix bugs and crashes, and to improve game balance and performance;</li>
      <li>To understand in aggregate how our Games are played, so we can decide what to build next;</li>
      <li>To show advertising in the Games, including, where permitted and where you have not opted out, advertising selected for you based on your interests;</li>
      <li>To answer your support requests;</li>
      <li>To detect and prevent cheating, fraud, and abuse;</li>
      <li>To comply with our legal obligations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Service providers we share information with</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information. We do share it with the service providers we rely on to operate the Games. The main ones are:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google Firebase</strong> (Google LLC) — used in many of our Games for analytics, crash reporting, and, in some Games, cloud storage of game progress and account identifiers. Google acts as our data processor for these services. See <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Firebase Privacy and Security</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Google AdMob and other advertising networks</strong> — used to select and deliver the ads shown in our Games, and to measure them. These networks receive your device’s advertising identifier and IP address. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Apple and Google</strong>, as the operators of the App Store and Google Play, which process purchases and provide store-level services such as Google Play Games sign-in.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may also disclose information where we are required to by law, to enforce our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>, or to protect the rights and safety of our users or of our company.</p>

    <h2>4. Advertising and your choices</h2>
    <p>Our Games are supported by advertising. Advertising networks may use your device’s advertising identifier to show you ads selected for your interests and to measure how ads perform. You can limit this at any time from your device:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Android:</strong> Settings → Google → Ads → Delete advertising ID, or Opt out of Ads Personalisation.</li>
      <li><strong>iOS:</strong> Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Tracking, and turn off Allow Apps to Request to Track.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Opting out does not remove advertising from the Games. It means the ads you see are less likely to be based on your interests. Some of our Games also offer a purchase that removes advertising; others do not.</p>

    <h2>5. Where your information is stored</h2>
    <p>We are based in the Republic of Korea. The service providers listed in section 3 operate servers in a number of countries, which means your information may be stored or processed outside the country where you live, including in the United States. Where this involves a transfer of personal data out of the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, our providers rely on transfer mechanisms approved under applicable law, such as the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses.</p>

    <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>Progress stored only on your device stays there until you delete the Game or clear its data, and we never hold a copy of it. Progress and account identifiers held on our servers are kept while your account remains active, and are deleted on request as described in section 7. Analytics and crash data are retained for a limited period under the default retention settings of the service concerned, and support emails are kept for as long as needed to resolve your request and to keep a record of it.</p>

    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to ask us for a copy of the personal information we hold about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to object to or restrict how we use it, and to withdraw consent you have given. Residents of the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom have these rights under the GDPR; residents of the Republic of Korea have equivalent rights under the Personal Information Protection Act.</p>
    <p>To make a request, email us at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. Please tell us which Game you play and, where the Game shows one, your in-game user ID, so that we can find the right records. We will respond within the period required by applicable law. You also have the right to complain to your local data protection authority.</p>

    <h2>8. Children</h2>
    <p>Our Games are intended for a general audience and are not directed at children under the age of 13 (or the equivalent minimum age in your country). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under that age. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> and we will delete it.</p>
    <p>Parents and guardians: the app store on your device provides parental controls that can restrict downloads and in-app purchases, and we encourage you to use them.</p>

    <h2>9. Security</h2>
    <p>We use a range of technical and organisational measures to protect information against loss, misuse, and unauthorised access, including encryption in transit and access controls on the systems that hold it. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, however, and the networks through which you reach our Games may be subject to failures outside our reasonable control, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

    <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the date at the top of this page, and where the change is significant we will give additional notice, such as a statement on this website or a notice inside the Game.</p>

    <h2>11. Contact us</h2>
    <p>Questions about this Privacy Policy, or about how we handle your information, can be sent to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. For general help with a Game, write to <a href="mailto:{{ site.supportEmail }}">{{ site.supportEmail }}</a>.</p>

